IMPORT prelude
IMPORT jurisdiction

§ `Currency Library`

-- Library for representing monetary amounts and currency codes
-- Uses ISO 4217 currency codes
-- Stores amounts as integer cents/minor units to avoid floating point errors
-- Version 1.0.0 (2024-12-16)

§§ `Version`

@nlg the version of the Currency Library
`Currency Library Version` MEANS "1.0.0"
@nlg the version date of the Currency Library
`Currency Library Date` MEANS "2024-12-16"


§§ `ISO 4217 Currency Codes`

-- Format: Currency name, code, numeric code, decimal places (minor units)

@nlg the ISO 4217 code for the US Dollar
`US Dollar code` MEANS "USD"
@nlg the ISO 4217 numeric code for the US Dollar
`US Dollar numeric` MEANS 840
@nlg the number of decimal places of the US Dollar
`US Dollar decimals` MEANS 2
@nlg the ISO 3166 alpha-2 code for the issuing country of the US Dollar
`US Dollar country` MEANS `United States alpha-2`

@nlg the ISO 4217 code for the Euro
`Euro code` MEANS "EUR"
@nlg the ISO 4217 numeric code for the Euro
`Euro numeric` MEANS 978
@nlg the number of decimal places of the Euro
`Euro decimals` MEANS 2
@nlg the code for the European Union as the region of the Euro
`Euro region` MEANS `European Union code`

@nlg the ISO 4217 code for the Pound Sterling
`British Pound code` MEANS "GBP"
@nlg the ISO 4217 numeric code for the Pound Sterling
`British Pound numeric` MEANS 826
@nlg the number of decimal places of the Pound Sterling
`British Pound decimals` MEANS 2
@nlg the ISO 3166 alpha-2 code for the issuing country of the Pound Sterling
`British Pound country` MEANS `United Kingdom alpha-2`

